# FH Inventory Project Rules

## Components

- Use **shadcn/ui** for all UI components. Add components via the shadcn CLI rather than building from scratch.
- **No single component file may exceed 400 lines.** Refactor into smaller components proactively — do not wait to be asked.

## Interaction & Visual Design

- Buttons and images must have a subtle **raise + drop shadow on hover**. Use the `.hover-lift` utility in `app/globals.css`.

## Responsive Design (Mobile-First)

- **Design mobile-first.** This app will be used predominantly on phones; desktop is secondary.
- Every screen must work well on small viewports before enhancing for larger breakpoints.
- Use touch-friendly targets (min ~44px tap area), readable text without zoom, and layouts that stack vertically on mobile.
- Prefer single-column layouts on mobile; use `sm:` / `md:` breakpoints only to add desktop enhancements.
- Test mentally (and in browser when possible) at ~375px width before considering a feature done.
